{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>וּאֻשַּׁיֵּהּ מְסֻבְּלַן</b> — like the matter of אבן גלל; and the meaning is: its foundations are carried in carrier-stones." "<b>רוּמֵהּ אַמִּין שִׁתִּין</b> — higher than Solomon's first building, for its height was thirty cubits, its stature." "<b>וְכֵן פְּתִיהּ אַמִּין שִׁתִּין</b> — because the height and the width are equal, and the length he did not mention, for it was like the first measure."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The Aramaic phrase ואושוהי מסובלין is from Ezra 6:3; אבן גלל appears to be a technical term for a type of stone, left untranslated as Ibn Ezra cites it."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:42:06.143040545Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}